  "body": "## Exact subject\n\n```text\nbase branch:               main\nbase commit:               968968046d69d000f1f9fe03683e92aa7903cf99\nbase tree:                 04ba2fab66dfc41680784e1288e14c2fc54c58d9\ncontent review predecessor: d5675aba3fc7b4d10bef9025b8c150784d38c129\none-shot bootstrap:        92a631c61036cc43351b7628e7334cec0068d995\ncontent materialization:   ea1d6f78df13b37fc27c4dfa0ac9b9c4d9544220\nworkflow rebind:           7953e8521bd30d298919917094501e01e012df14\nparser hardening:          c5d25e796a6aea825a8728e5a6ca96c7c43da14f\nfinal no-content rebind:   b8e875d8d01893d894ae0666db9e4efdcc106d59\nhead tree:                 ea88df68fd404273c32442c45539054b4fcc4d54\ncommits from base:         11\nchanged paths from base:   25\n```\n\n`main` and the repository default integration branch identify the same base commit. Movement of the base, final head/tree, prospective merge, workflow object, generated status or review surface invalidates exact-object admission and requires a fresh terminal packet and review.\n\nThe final commit is a user-authored, no-content rebind to the exact parser-hardening tree because GitHub suppressed pull-request workflows on the materializer-authored commit. No reviewed source byte changed between `c5d25e796...` and `b8e875d8...`.\n\n## Change class and boundaries\n\n- Change class: D3 repository/component lifecycle and qualification gate.\n- Affected logical modules: all modules indirectly through concrete component inventory; no production runtime API, state schema, ordering, resource budget or effect behavior changes.\n- Compatibility: source/documentation additive; no wire or durable-state migration.\n- Rollback: revert this PR; no installed target or external effect is created.\n\n## Complete closure scope\n\n- give every one of the 24 root Cargo workspace members a component-local technical README;\n- preserve the exact split of 11 active default-source components and 13 sealed non-product components;\n- add a normative component development standard and a fail-closed executable verifier;\n- require each README to identify its exact Cargo package and expose the exact visible shell command `cargo test --locked -p <package> --all-targets`;\n- require each active component to expose visible links to all physically derivable module contracts while permitting only explicit conceptual links to registered module IDs;\n- reject HTML-comment evidence, unterminated comments, inline-code substitutes, non-shell or indented-code command substitutes, fenced/indented navigation, escaped/remote/absolute/query/fragment/percent-encoded targets, wrong relative paths, `.md` disguises and symlink traversal;\n- retain multiline inline-code state across physical lines so a hidden module link cannot regain visible-link credit;\n- evaluate indentation in CommonMark columns so tab or mixed-tab faux fences cannot regain shell-command credit;\n- aggregate all component README command/contract failures so all 24 members are evaluated in one run;\n- retain strict workspace/lifecycle set equality, package identity, UTF-8/size bounds, duplicate JSON/package/module rejection and normalized path checks;\n- register the complete live diff in `governance/pr41-review-index.v1.json` with byte-exact path/change digests;\n- retain generated component status registration, protected-main wording and explicit no-target/no-device/no-release authority claims.\n\n## Verification already executed\n\nThe final two-file parser repair was applied only after an exact head/tree lease and passed:\n\n```text\n27/27 focused component-documentation tests\npython3 tools/docs/verify_component_documentation.py\npython3 tools/docs/generate_global_docs.py --check\npython3 tools/docs/verify_global_docs.py\npython3 -m py_compile <changed verifier/tests>\ngit diff --check\n```\n\nFresh permanent exact-head and synthetic-merge workflows remain authoritative for `b8e875d8...`; local/materializer success is not substituted for those results.\n\n## Review slices\n\n- `runtime-and-protocol`: `Tomasrgbsf`, including component-local source commands and module-contract mapping;\n- `ci-evidence-and-authority`, `documentation-and-contracts`, `repository-and-retirement`, `source-tooling-and-verification`: `Franksudoman`;\n- accountable author/owner: `ProfHepta`; no self-review is assigned.\n\nAll approvals or change requests on older heads remain historical. Fresh non-author review must bind `b8e875d8d01893d894ae0666db9e4efdcc106d59` and the current prospective merge after the complete workflow matrix reaches terminal success.\n\n## Risk and performance\n\n- Runtime/SLO impact: none expected; no product source or Cargo graph changed.\n- CI risk: stricter Markdown parsing can expose previously hidden README defects; the checked-in workspace passes the verifier.\n- Security posture: final tree contains no materializer, write token, persisted checkout credential or branch-push logic introduced by the repair.\n\n## Explicit negative claims\n\nThis PR grants no installed Root Linux, installed Codex, Android target-files/image, physical-device, destructive-fault, signing, deployment, OTA or public-release authority. `automatic_redispatch=false`, `zero_gap=false` and `public_release=false` remain unchanged. L2–L6 still require independently produced target evidence under issue #22.",
